---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro"
import VerdictBadge from "../components/VerdictBadge.astro"
import { VERDICTS, VERDICT_NAMES } from "../site"
---

<Page
  title="Methodology"
  description="How SnarkBrain chooses claims to check, the sources we rely on, how fact-checks are structured, what each verdict means and how we correct mistakes."
  lede="How we choose claims, what counts as evidence, and what our verdicts mean."
>
  <h2>What we check</h2>
  <p>
    We check specific, verifiable claims about Ethan Klein, Hila Klein and the H3 Podcast that are circulating publicly
    — on Reddit, YouTube, TikTok, X and elsewhere. We focus on claims the record can confirm or refute.
  </p>

  <h2>What counts as evidence</h2>
  <p>We rely on primary sources wherever they exist:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>full episodes and streams, linked at the exact timestamp being discussed;</li>
    <li>court filings and other public records;</li>
    <li>original posts and statements from the people involved.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where a primary source is at risk of disappearing, we host a copy alongside the fact-check. Reference material and
    news reporting are cited for general facts and background, such as medical or legal context.
  </p>

  <h2>How a fact-check is structured</h2>
  <p>Every fact-check follows the same format, so you can find what you need quickly:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>The claim and verdict</strong>, summarized at the top.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Background</strong>: the context needed to understand where the claim came from.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Claim</strong>: stated the way its proponents state it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Truth</strong>: what the record shows, point by point, with a numbered citation for each statement.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Conclusion</strong>: what the evidence adds up to.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>References</strong>: every source, in order.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Verdicts</h2>
  <dl class="verdicts">
    {VERDICT_NAMES.map(v => (
      <div>
        <dt>
          <VerdictBadge verdict={v} />
        </dt>
        <dd>{VERDICTS[v].summary}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2>Dates and updates</h2>
  <p>
    Each fact-check shows the date it was published and, when it has been materially revised, the date of its latest
    update.
  </p>

  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If a fact-check contains a factual error, we correct it and add a dated note at the bottom of the page explaining
    what changed. If new evidence changes a verdict, the verdict is updated and noted the same way. Typos, formatting
    and broken links are fixed without a note.
  </p>
  <p>
    To report an error, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> with the page, the statement you believe is wrong and any
    evidence.
  </p>
</Page>

<style>
  .verdicts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .verdicts div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .verdicts dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .verdicts div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
